MarcelInTO__glute	R1	When pushing to or cloning a GitHub repo over HTTPS on this machine, embed the gh CLI token in the URL (https://x-access-token:$(gh auth token)@github.com/<owner>/<repo>.git) instead of relying on git's credential helper.
MarcelInTO__glute	R2	For a one-off GitHub push, clone the repo using the token URL into the scratchpad directory.
MarcelInTO__glute	R3	After a one-off GitHub push, remove the scratchpad clone, since the token is stored in its .git/config.
MarcelInTO__glute	R4	Do not install the libsecret credential helper to fix GitHub HTTPS auth failures without first asking the user.
MarcelInTO__glute	R5	When glute hangs, send `kill -USR1 <pid>` to the process before doing anything else.
MarcelInTO__glute	R6	After sending `kill -USR1`, read the goroutine dump in `glute.log` before killing the glute process.
MarcelInTO__glute	R7	If a killed glute run leaves the terminal in raw mode, run `reset` to restore it.
MarcelInTO__glute	R8	Build new stats features on the GraphQL client in `internal/gitlab/graphql.go`, not on new REST paths.
MarcelInTO__glute	R9	When designing stats features, do not expect GitLab's GraphQL to aggregate server-side. Pull the records and aggregate them client-side.
MarcelInTO__glute	R10	Make sure projects that are alive only through forgotten scheduled pipelines are never skipped by the resync or poll logic.
MarcelInTO__glute	R11	Do not gate the warm per-project sweep on `last_activity_at`.
MarcelInTO__glute	R12	Do not use the group-level GraphQL `projects { pipelines(first:1, updatedAfter) }` query in the warm sweep. Use it only for a once-per-resync probe.
MarcelInTO__glute	R13	Land glute work on the `main` branch.
MarcelInTO__glute	R14	When working on a performance task, instrument the running app and gather real measurements before designing any optimization.
MarcelInTO__glute	R15	For a nontrivial performance task, add lightweight per-phase timing/counters first, retained across runs and surfaced somewhere observable, then run against a realistic dataset and let the breakdown choose the optimization target.
MarcelInTO__glute	R16	After a performance optimization, keep the instrumentation in place to confirm the improvement.
MarcelInTO__glute	R17	Do not trust prior claims that a particular part is the slow part, including claims written in the repo's own docs; verify with measurement.
